@startuml
hide circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title Smart Campus - domain class diagram (revised)

enum BookingStatus {
  ACTIVE
  CANCELLED
}

class Student {
  studentId : String
  name : String
}

class Room {
  roomId : String
  name : String
  blocked : Boolean
  block()
  unblock()
}

class Booking {
  bookingId : String
  start : DateTime
  end : DateTime
  status : BookingStatus
  cancel()
}

class Confirmation {
  confirmationId : String
  issuedAt : DateTime
}

Student "1" -- "0..*" Booking : makes >
Booking "0..*" -- "1" Room : reserves >
Booking "1" -- "1" Confirmation : produces >

note right of Booking
  R1: start is in the future and
  0 < (end - start) <= 2 hours.
  R2: two ACTIVE bookings for the same room
  must not overlap. Time is [start, end), so
  10:00-12:00 and 12:00-13:00 do not overlap (A1).
  US-03: only the student who made the booking
  can cancel it; cancel() sets status = CANCELLED.
end note

note bottom of Room
  R3: blocked = true means no NEW booking.
  Bookings that already exist stay ACTIVE (A2).
end note

note bottom of Confirmation
  R4 / US-04: created only for a successful booking.
  Cancellation confirmation is out of scope (A5).
end note
@enduml
